  "Study.Name": "Longitudinal Recovery Processes and Daily Experience Study",
  "authors": "Dr. Sarah Johnson, Dr. Michael Chen, Dr. Lisa Rodriguez, Dr. James Thompson",
  "funding": "NIH National Institute on Drug Abuse Grant R01DA045678; Substance Abuse and Mental Health Services Administration Grant TI123456",
  "abstract": "This intensive longitudinal study examines the daily processes and contextual factors associated with substance use recovery. Participants completed a comprehensive baseline assessment followed by ecological momentary assessments (EMA) 10 times daily for 30 days. The study investigates temporal patterns of craving, affect, stress, coping strategies, social context, and substance use in real-world settings to identify proximal predictors of relapse and recovery milestones.",
